Z||000000||dgroves||12-18-2001||10:26 AM||||After 2 months of tinkering and cleaning and painting and writing checks, Fiero ('86 GT) is on the road. $300 car is now $3000 car but what a gas! All new engine parts + .040 over. 3.1 liter crank and Crane 2030 cam. Did standard head, plentum and exaust mods. Tranny, axles and rear brake calipers and pads are new also. I had reservations about the cost but now that I have driven the car with the above described modifications, my only comment is WOW. Pontiac should have made um this way to start with. The car is sooooo responsive. The new motor pulls so strong from idle to 4700. (That's as tight as I have spun it so far.) And the sound it makes.......! (No cat)Can't wait till break in is over. It's clear to me now just what FIERO is all about. Thanks to PFF for all the advice and help. Would have been much tougher to complete without somewhere to get questions answered.||||reg||6
