Z||000003||Smoooooth GT||12-18-2001||01:38 PM||||Sound's like a GREAT $300.00 car...lol  Do you know how much HP you gained adding the Larger Crank.. and the Crane Cam?? What does your A$$ Meter read??  lol  Steve<BR>OOoohh Pic's please!!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SNOWMAN_MELTING.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/vroom_5.gif">        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">                  <BR>      <P> <A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A> <P>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||14
Z||000004||dgroves||12-19-2001||01:10 AM||||Things get better... Did Joe Torma's idle adjustment procedure today and car is idling at 850 in gear  and 1000/1100 in park. Changed break in oil today after 180 miles. Some color in last few spoon fulls. New filter. Found TCC brake connection loose. Was reason lock up wasn't working.<P>Did somebody ask about seat of the pants dyno? Well, it's quite satisfying. I didn't intend to build a race car, I just wanted something responsive and good looking to do my daily driving with. Good mileage, individualistic, able to f**k with a 5.0 Mustang at stoplights he. he. Well, I got it in SPADES. In traffic today, I could get in any spot that left me more than a couple of feet. Below 20 MPH it literaly leaps when max pedal is applied. No wheelspin, just GO! Haven't gone on Interstate but once yet. From 60 or so with tcc locked, apply throttle without disengaging lock up (about 3/4) and car accelerates to 80 before an "Old Man" can react. Scheduled for an alignment in the morning. Car is "Loose" now because of camber mis alignment from cradle removal. (Kinda fun in the rain but DANGEROUS)<P>Not sure how to put pics up but will figgure out. I took some with film and some with digital.<P>Drive On<P>86GT 3.1 etc....... ||||reg||6
